A destroy that leaves a thread blocked on a notification it took away.
The thread waits on an object that is no longer live.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: queue holds something that is not a thread
Report: thread waits on something that is not a notification

diff --git a/kernel/pool.c b/kernel/pool.c
--- a/kernel/pool.c
+++ b/kernel/pool.c
@@ -48,7 +48,6 @@ static void pool_clear(struct pool *pool)
     for (struct obj_header *o = pool_first(pool), *next; o != NULL; o = next) {
         LOOP_PAID(pool_clear, object, "an object of the pool that goes");
         next = pool_next(pool, o);
-        sched_forget(o);
         CALL_BOUND(OBJ_MAX_SIZE);
         memset(o, 0, obj_size(o));
     }
